 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "71:11-17 (the rhetorical «ونرد على أعقابنا») is not glossed, so the question is never shown as a statement. Two paths for the bewildered one, no person and no motif on the devils; light for «إن هدى الله هو الهدى». Stars for the heavens, geometric for «عالم الغيب والشهادة». The Horn (73:16-18): nothing drawn. 73: short-word flag, listen. STAGING v4: c1: the believers (Al-Muyassar: the command includes all of us) refuse at 71:2 to invoke what neither benefits nor harms; the rhetorical turning back (71:11-13) is not acted. The parable (71:18-29): a lone traveller led astray in the land, bewildered (two quick turns on 71:23 and 71:25, a two-paths plate), his companions call him to guidance (71:26); he does not turn his back on them. His refusal is not drawn (only Al-Muyassar says he refuses; As-Sa'di says he stays bewildered between the two callers). The devils are never drawn. The light plate starts on 71:35, after the Name. c2 stays ambient (the Gathering, creation, the Day, the Horn, His attributes) with a hands plate for the prayer (72:2)."
 },
